# diff-openbsd set `syscalls` (format: tools/xtask/src/diffopenbsd/scenario.rs): the system
# call probes of tools/difftest, section by section, in one directory of the scratch file
# system (`setup` mounted it on /mnt). Each probe prints its return value or `-1 ENAME`, so a
# different errno is a different line. Probes that hit an unported part of EmiBSD (fifofs,
# exec_script.c, file mappings) have sections of their own, so that their expected
# difference (expected.toml) cannot hide another one. `tty` (N4.7) follows `ostype`, so no
# step id of expected.toml moves: pairs from /dev/ptm, the line discipline, the session's
# terminal, sendsyslog(2) and kern.tty.

## probes
! mkdir /mnt/sc
! cd /mnt/sc
$ difftest syscalls files
$ difftest syscalls dirs
$ difftest syscalls links
$ difftest syscalls fifo
$ difftest syscalls perms
$ difftest syscalls procs
$ difftest syscalls signals
$ difftest syscalls script
$ difftest syscalls ipc
$ difftest syscalls kqueue
$ difftest syscalls memory
$ difftest syscalls mmapfile
$ difftest syscalls sysctl
$ difftest syscalls ostype
$ difftest syscalls tty
$ ls -1a
! cd /

## coredump
! mkdir /mnt/core
! cd /mnt/core
$ sh -c 'ulimit -c unlimited; kill -SEGV $$'; echo status $?; ls -1
! cd /
! rm -rf /mnt/core

## entry
# The system call entry's checks (N4.8b), each in a child with no controlling terminal and
# no core file, its end printed: a call with the stack pointer pivoted off MAP_STACK
# (stackpivot: SIGSEGV), SYS_getpid with bit 32 set in x8 (int-syscall: the number is an int,
# the unpinned site SIGABRT), a plain unpinned SYS_getpid (unpinned-svc: SIGABRT). arm64 only
# (amd64's at N10); it writes no file, so it runs where it is. A set of its own after
# coredump, so no step id of expected.toml moves; this one is syscalls/entry#1.
$ difftest syscalls entry
